    <briefdescription>
<para>The GSYM header. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The GSYM header is found at the start of a stand alone GSYM file, or as the first bytes in a section when GSYM is contained in a section of an executable file (<ref refid="namespacellvm_1_1_e_l_f" kindref="compound">ELF</ref>, mach-o, <ref refid="namespacellvm_1_1_c_o_f_f" kindref="compound">COFF</ref>).</para>
<para>The structure is encoded exactly as it appears in the structure definition with no gaps between members. Alignment should not change from system to system as the members were laid out so that they shouldn&apos;t align differently on different architectures.</para>
<para>When endianness of the system loading a GSYM file matches, the file can be mmap&apos;ed in and a pointer to the header can be cast to the first bytes of the file (stand alone GSYM file) or section data (GSYM in a section). When endianness is swapped, the <ref refid="structllvm_1_1gsym_1_1_header_1a3e167f635eebf81005b8ac7290195165" kindref="member">Header::decode()</ref> function should be used to decode the header. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
